// Title: Weak or Abused Passwords In CLI
// ID: 91edcfb1-2529-4ac2-9ecc-7617f895c7e4
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-14
// Tags: attack.execution, attack.stealth
// Description: Detects weak passwords or often abused passwords (seen used by threat actors) via the CLI.
// An example would be a threat actor creating a new user via the net command and providing the password inline
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where ((process.command_line like "*_123456789*" or process.command_line like "*_123123qwE*" or process.command_line like "*_Asd123.aaaa*" or process.command_line like "*_Decryptme*" or process.command_line like "*_P@ssw0rd!*" or process.command_line like "*_Pass8080*" or process.command_line like "*_password123*" or process.command_line like "*_test@202*"))
